WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.480
You think this sort of thing will actually work?

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.860
It's probably just for the benefit of the media.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.740
After all, we need to show them that the police are doing their job too.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.910
H-Hey! L-Look over there!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.160
You're Takeda Shunsuke!

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.670
Stop right there!

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.510
Is it true that Goto-san is missing?

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.980
Let's look for him together.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.770
And if that isn't enough, we can ask Yakumo-san to help as well, and-

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.280
I haven't been able to reach Yakumo-shi either...

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.370
Well, have you tried calling that girl then? You know, Ozawa Haruka-san?

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.620
I don't know her number...

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.000
What is it?

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.170
Is that... Goto-san's?

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.260
They say that fate is a strange thing,

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.020
but to think that all those that are connected to Yakumo would be gathered here today...

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.570
To begin with, allow me to introduce myself.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.240
I'm Yakumo's uncle, Isshin.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.160
I heard that Yakumo-san's left eye is red as well,

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.240
can you also use that left eye to-

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.660
Um, actually his eye is-

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.710
Haruka-chan.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.710
Sorry...

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.880
I'm sorry.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.920
We were introducing ourselves, weren't we?

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.420
I'm Hijikata Makoto from the Hokuto Press Company.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.680
And this is Ishii Yutaro-san from the Seta City Police.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.190
Then let us move on to the reason why we're all gathered here today.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.070
Yakumo and Goto-kun both disappeared around the same time,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.610
and both of them watched the tape of the ghost

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.700
filmed at the scene of the Nanase murders 15 years ago, am I correct?

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.700
Yes.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.700
May I see that tape please?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.010
Th-That's...

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.180
I-Isshin-san?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.680
Is something wrong?

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.810
I knew it.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.190
There's no doubt about it.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.110
This is... my sister.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.110
That's Azusa.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.030
Yakumo-kun's mother?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.870
I'm sure it gave Yakumo a shock.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:12.670
Azusa went missing 15 years ago. If she's been caught on tape as a ghost now,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.000
then that means that she's already...

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.090
Let's just stop this.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.680
This is useless.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.390
We should just leave everything to the police.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.400
Ishii-san...

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.480
They're already searching for Detective Goto.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.990
As for Yakumo-shi, we just need to file a missing persons report.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.070
It's pointless for us to look into this ourselves.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.410
Ishii-san!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.410
So, just because you think it's pointless, you're not going to do anything?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.410
You think that we should just leave everything for someone else to handle?

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.120
H-Haruka-chan...

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.540
I don't want to wait!

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.210
I won't just pass things on for other people to do!

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.460
I will never give up!

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.420
Not until I find Yakumo-kun...

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.430
Ishii-san, you disgust me!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.230
Ishii-san!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.200
Please don't be so kind to someone like me. It just makes it worse.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.550
You know, I misjudged her.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:46.340
When I first met her, I assumed she was just an ordinary but somewhat cute girl.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.720
She's not just somewhat cute, she's really cute.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.230
Instead, I discovered that behind her appearance lies a very strong-hearted girl.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.860
"Never give up."

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.110
Don't you think that's a really wonderful attitude to have?

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.450
When I was a child, I wanted to be a manga artist.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.710
But I soon gave that up...

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.040
because my father objected.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.750
What does your father do?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.380
He's a police officer.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.380
He's a very stern man.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.760
It wasn't just about being a manga artist either.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.050
In fact, he suppressed my individuality.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.560
Do you hate your father?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.730
My father is wrong in his thinking,

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.560
but so am I for blindly following his orders.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.070
If you realize that, then all that remains is for you to make your move.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.410
Make my move?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.950
Yes, it's time for you to make your move.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:57.580
Even if it doesn't pay off or you're laughed at, go down the path that <i>you</i> believe is right.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.830
Makoto-san...

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:07.050
Until we find Yakumo-san and Detective Goto, why don't we both try our best?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.090
Let's also try to never give up.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.600
Those glasses...

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.570
My eyes have been opened.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:26.110
From now on, I'll try to do what Detective Goto would.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.490
Okay.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.120
So this is where you went.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.130
Yes.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.380
I guess coincidences like this happen as well...

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.840
Or perhaps...

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.010
Takagishi Akemi-san.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:55.390
She was Yakumo's middle school teacher.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.890
It's been five years since she passed away.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:04.190
That day, Yakumo...

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.820
It's all my fault.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:19.580
She died because of my red left eye.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.620
Stop this craziness.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:04.960
I'm sure there's a really good reason why you can see ghosts.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.290
Don't run from your fate.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.970
My eye brings suffering to others,

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.130
and I too, am suffering.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:20.140
Then I shall also walk the path where others will view me with wary eyes.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.640
Why?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.270
Why do you and her go to such lengths for my sake?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.650
How can you, for someone who was even abandoned by his own mother?!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.490
Nobody is alone.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.570
Everyone is bound by the strings of fate.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.660
I'm positive that there's someone out there for you too.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:43.660
Someday, someone will appear who will see your red eye as something beautiful.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.130
There will never be anyone like that!

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:50.670
And even if there is, I can only bring them suffering...

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:10.690
When I first met him, there was something about him that automatically pushed people away.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:17.700
But behind his facade, he was secretly hoping to avoid bringing harm and suffering to others.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.790
You should ask Yakumo for the details.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.830
As he is now, I'm certain he'll tell you.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.710
But before you can do that, you need to find him, right?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.210
Yes.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.890
Ishii-san.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.480
Please forgive my rudeness.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.980
No, it's fine...

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.900
I'm also sorry for saying something so mean to you.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.910
Think like Yakumo-kun would?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.240
What do you mean?

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:08.670
I believe that Yakumo-san found a clue by watching that footage.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:12.000
In order to figure out what that clue was, we need to think like he would.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.760
Let's go over all his actions from when he watched the footage.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:23.760
I remember now!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.020
Yakumo-shi was studying a map of the area surrounding the Nanase residence.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:33.070
When Goto-san told me to fast forward the tape, he objected and overruled him, didn't he?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.530
The train tracks?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.550
I knew it!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:03.640
We can't hear any trains passing by in the background of that footage.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.930
However, that house is near the train tracks,

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.810
and when that footage was filmed,

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.480
there should've been a train passing approximately every seven minutes.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.980
In other words, this footage is...

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:18.490
It's highly likely that it was actually filmed elsewhere.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.700
He must have realized this.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:26.740
Then Hoshino Yukiko-san, who gave me this footage, is...

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.250
Takeda Shunsuke has made his move?

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.120
Yes.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.500
I will head to where Yakumo is.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.340
Got it.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.510
I'll grab that Ozawa Haruka girl.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.020
I see.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.270
Thank you very much.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.520
How did it go?

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:58.400
There is no woman named Hoshino Yukiko employed by that company.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.530
It's the same story over here.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.030
The address she gave when she was hospitalized is a fake.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:09.540
Haruka-chan!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.710
What's wrong?

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.460
Your surname if I remember correctly is Ozawa, right?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.420
Yes.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.710
Does your family by any chance live in Nagano?

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.550
Yes, they do.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.550
And your mother is Keiko-san, correct?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:29.970
Um, why are you suddenly bringing up my mother's name?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:34.270
This was a letter sent to my sister a long time ago.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.820
No way!

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.950
What's wrong?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.740
My mother wrote this letter.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.740
Really?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:51.750
The strings of fate are connected.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.250
When she was young, my sister Azusa was abducted by a man

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.050
and held captive in a villa within the forest of Nagano.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.550
And when she finally escaped after two weeks...

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.180
So that woman was my mother...

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:20.770
She was worried about my sister, so she continued to keep in touch with her even after the event.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.990
And so, the two of them often wrote to each other.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.450
This is really a miraculous fate.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.410
Perhaps Yakumo and Haruka-chan

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.620
were bound to each other by an invisible bond even before their births.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.040
An invisible bond?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:44.010
Apparently Keiko-san was already pregnant with Haruka-chan at the time.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.800
Furthermore, Yakumo also existed...

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.640
My sister was pregnant with Yakumo.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.730
His father is...

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.770
the man who abducted and confined Azusa.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.320
That means...

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.070
That's terrible...

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.080
Does Yakumo-kun know about this?

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:18.080
I told him a while back, so that the same mistakes wouldn't be repeated.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.580
Mistakes?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:28.590
When Yakumo-kun was a child, Azusa-san almost...

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:37.180
At the time, Goto-san worked at a police box. He's the one who saved Yakumo-kun.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:41.690
Azusa-san has been missing ever since.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:47.820
More importantly, we received that letter soon after Azusa tried to kill Yakumo.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.740
I've tried to open that letter many times...

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.080
Hoping that it would offer some clues to finding my sister...

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.710
But in the end, I never can.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.210
Why not?

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:17.180
So for Isshin-san, this letter is something of a Pandora's box. It's something that must not be opened.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.440
If the real reason behind why Azusa-san tried to kill her biological son,

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.650
is written within that letter...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:31.740
If I were in Isshin-san's shoes, I wouldn't have the courage to tell Yakumo-shi.

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.530
But...

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:39.870
If it really is Pandora's box, you should find hope at the very end.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.220
Saito Azusa-sama,

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:56.260
It may be a little early, but congratulations on your wedding.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:02.390
Even though a lot has happened to you, I hope the three of you, including Yakumo-kun, live a happy life.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.400
I'm really happy for you.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.400
P.S.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.740
"P.S. I read Takeda-san's articles.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.070
It's so cool that he's a journalist.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:16.990
Please give my kind wishes to your handsome fiancé, Takeda Shunsuke-san."

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:16.990
What?!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.040
Azusa-san's fiancé was...

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.540
Takeda Shunsuke, the man who murdered the Nanase family!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:35.180
We're returning to the station to re-investigate the case.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.430
Okay.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:41.310
I'll call my mother and ask her.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:54.320
That reminds me, I've hardly slept since Yakumo-kun went missing.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.370
I can't...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.830
I can't sleep.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.670
I need to call my mother.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.300
Give up, Takeda!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.810
H-He disappeared...

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:26.690
Say that one more time and I-

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.520
I will repeat myself as many times as necessary!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.320
I want to examine all the reports on Takeda Shunsuke and any related documents

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.200
in order to assist my search for Detective Goto-

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.570
Can you stop being so violent please?!

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.740
Shut up!

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.330
Right now, we're really busy.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.700
Meaning?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.710
Takeda Shunsuke has been located.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.750
Really?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.000
We're currently pursuing him.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.050
I understand your current situation,

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:59.970
but my mission is to find Detective Goto.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.220
Please! I'm begging you!

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.600
A newbie should know his place.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.640
Listen closely.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:10.810
I hear the men's washroom on the fourth floor needs cleaning.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.940
Go and clean it right now.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.450
Make sure you pay special attention to the furthest stall.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.450
It's really dirty behind the toilet tank.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.240
I'll check them later, so make sure you do a good job.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.870
Understand?

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.250
Behind the toilet tank, understand?

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.250
Understood. I'll clean the washroom.

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:45.310
Well then, I think I'll have a conversation with myself.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.640
Captain Miyagawa.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.480
Who the hell replies to someone talking to themselves?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.900
Just shut up and listen.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:57.490
Don't talk to any of the investigators from back then. It'll only cause trouble.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.070
As long as they're not from the police, I don't mind who you talk to.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:06.330
And it was that disgusting old geezer who performed the autopsies back then.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.540
Hata-san, eh?

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.210
And-

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:12.170
I'll talk to Detective Goto's wife.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.040
Okay.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.590
I'm solely responsible for this.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.430
Put your broken glasses on my tab.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.550
I'll pay you back eventually.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.510
Yes, Ma'am.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:28.680
Since we've located Takeda, I'll have my hands full with him.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.020
I'm counting on you, Ishii.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.980
No matter what, find Goto.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:32.730
Yes, Ma'am!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:37.570
Um... this is the men's washroom...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.700
Yes, it's the first time I've been in one.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:48.080
Yes. No matter what, I'll find Detective Goto.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.580
Please believe in me and wait.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.460
Please take care of my husband.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:03.220
Ozawa Haruka, I've come to pick you up.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:09.390
I shall ruin you bit by bit, right in front of Yakumo.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:13.980
And you shall die in fear and desperation.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.110
Now then, let's go...

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.070
to Yakumo.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.200
Wait.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.950
Takeda Shunsuke.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.960
I know what you are.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:40.880
You can't stop me.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.800
Because you're a...

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:52.680
So your aim was to mobilize the police and prevent my movements.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.770
It's true that I'm powerless,

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:59.770
